{"lines": [{"text": "On March ninth, twenty twenty-three, customers pulled forty-two billion dollars out of one single bank. In one day.", "start": 0.6, "end": 7.752, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-98, 39, 1.0], "cam2": [-121.96, 37.35, 6.5], "pins": [{"at": [-121.96, 37.35], "label": "Silicon Valley Bank", "col": "red"}], "counter": {"to": 42, "pre": "−$", "suf": "B", "label": "withdrawn on March 9"}, "title": ["$42 BILLION", "OUT OF ONE BANK – IN ONE DAY"], "mood": "tense"}, "words": [["On", 0.093, 0.185], ["March", 0.185, 0.474], ["ninth", 0.475, 0.926], ["twenty", 1.1, 1.343], ["twenty-three", 1.343, 1.956], ["customers", 2.361, 2.778], ["pulled", 2.778, 3.056], ["forty-two", 3.067, 3.634], ["billion", 3.646, 4.005], ["dollars", 4.005, 4.56], ["out", 4.653, 4.803], ["of", 4.803, 4.884], ["one", 4.884, 5.185], ["single", 5.185, 5.451], ["bank", 5.451, 5.833], ["In", 6.215, 6.308], ["one", 6.319, 6.47], ["day", 6.47, 6.794]]}, {"text": "The next morning, another hundred billion was lined up to leave. And by lunchtime, the bank was gone.", "start": 8.152, "end": 13.672, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-121.96, 37.35, 6.5], "pins": [{"at": [-121.96, 37.35], "label": "Silicon Valley Bank", "col": "red", "closed": true}], "counter": {"from_": 42, "to": 142, "pre": "−$", "suf": "B", "label": "lined up to leave"}}, "words": [["The", 0.08, 0.114], ["next", 0.125, 0.352], ["morning", 0.352, 0.784], ["another", 1.045, 1.318], ["hundred", 1.33, 1.58], ["billion", 1.58, 1.989], ["was", 2.125, 2.25], ["lined", 2.25, 2.489], ["up", 2.489, 2.591], ["to", 2.591, 2.67], ["leave", 2.682, 3.136], ["And", 3.489, 3.545], ["by", 3.545, 3.648], ["lunchtime", 3.648, 4.227], ["the", 4.42, 4.5], ["bank", 4.511, 4.761], ["was", 4.761, 4.875], ["gone", 4.886, 5.205]]}, {"text": "So what actually happens to your money when your bank collapses? And could it happen to your bank, too?", "start": 14.222, "end": 19.214, "spec": {"type": "img", "img": 1, "chips": ["Your money?", "Your bank?"]}, "words": [["So", 0.091, 0.216], ["what", 0.227, 0.341], ["actually", 0.352, 0.636], ["happens", 0.636, 1.034], ["to", 1.045, 1.136], ["your", 1.136, 1.239], ["money", 1.239, 1.614], ["when", 1.784, 1.886], ["your", 1.886, 2.0], ["bank", 2.0, 2.239], ["collapses", 2.25, 2.92], ["And", 3.284, 3.386], ["could", 3.534, 3.648], ["it", 3.648, 3.693], ["happen", 3.693, 3.943], ["to", 3.955, 4.023], ["your", 4.023, 4.102], ["bank", 4.114, 4.398], ["too", 4.409, 4.659]]}, {"text": "To understand that, you first need to know one slightly uncomfortable secret about banks.", "start": 19.614, "end": 25.038, "spec": {"type": "img", "img": 2, "mood": "calm"}, "words": [["To", 0.091, 0.148], ["understand", 0.148, 0.625], ["that", 0.625, 0.898], ["you", 1.102, 1.216], ["first", 1.227, 1.489], ["need", 1.489, 1.614], ["to", 1.614, 1.67], ["know", 1.682, 2.159], ["one", 2.307, 2.591], ["slightly", 2.602, 3.273], ["uncomfortable", 3.284, 3.955], ["secret", 3.955, 4.352], ["about", 4.352, 4.602], ["banks", 4.602, 5.091]]}, {"text": "When you put a thousand dollars into your account, the bank doesn't just keep it in a vault.", "start": 25.438, "end": 29.566, "spec": {"type": "bank", "step": "deposit"}, "words": [["When", 0.091, 0.148], ["you", 0.159, 0.216], ["put", 0.216, 0.341], ["a", 0.341, 0.375], ["thousand", 0.386, 0.909], ["dollars", 0.909, 1.227], ["into", 1.227, 1.375], ["your", 1.375, 1.511], ["account", 1.523, 1.92], ["the", 2.148, 2.25], ["bank", 2.261, 2.591], ["doesn't", 2.67, 2.966], ["just", 2.966, 3.136], ["keep", 3.136, 3.318], ["it", 3.318, 3.352], ["in", 3.352, 3.42], ["a", 3.42, 3.443], ["vault", 3.443, 3.795]]}, {"text": "It lends most of it out to people buying homes and cars, or invests it in things like government bonds.", "start": 29.966, "end": 35.558, "spec": {"type": "bank", "step": "lend"}, "words": [["It", 0.091, 0.17], ["lends", 0.17, 0.364], ["most", 0.364, 0.648], ["of", 0.659, 0.705], ["it", 0.705, 0.75], ["out", 0.75, 0.932], ["to", 0.932, 1.011], ["people", 1.011, 1.364], ["buying", 1.375, 1.739], ["homes", 1.75, 2.159], ["and", 2.159, 2.239], ["cars", 2.25, 2.83], ["or", 3.045, 3.273], ["invests", 3.477, 3.886], ["it", 3.886, 3.943], ["in", 3.955, 4.034], ["things", 4.045, 4.33], ["like", 4.341, 4.443], ["government", 4.443, 4.773], ["bonds", 4.773, 5.239]]}, {"text": "In the US, banks don't even have to keep a minimum share in reserve anymore. Since March twenty twenty, that requirement is zero percent.", "start": 35.958, "end": 44.19, "spec": {"type": "bank", "step": "zero"}, "words": [["In", 0.08, 0.148], ["the", 0.148, 0.182], ["US", 0.182, 0.818], ["banks", 1.011, 1.364], ["don't", 1.375, 1.545], ["even", 1.545, 1.67], ["have", 1.67, 1.864], ["to", 1.864, 1.932], ["keep", 1.932, 2.136], ["a", 2.148, 2.182], ["minimum", 2.182, 2.682], ["share", 2.682, 3.159], ["in", 3.295, 3.409], ["reserve", 3.42, 3.716], ["anymore", 3.716, 4.193], ["Since", 4.557, 4.784], ["March", 4.795, 5.091], ["twenty", 5.102, 5.364], ["twenty", 5.375, 5.727], ["that", 5.955, 6.091], ["requirement", 6.102, 6.693], ["is", 6.75, 6.909], ["zero", 7.011, 7.352], ["percent", 7.352, 7.898]]}, {"text": "And that works perfectly well, as long as not everyone wants their money back on the same day.", "start": 44.59, "end": 49.51, "spec": {"type": "bank", "step": "run"}, "words": [["And", 0.091, 0.193], ["that", 0.33, 0.5], ["works", 0.5, 0.75], ["perfectly", 0.761, 1.284], ["well", 1.284, 1.67], ["as", 1.932, 2.057], ["long", 2.057, 2.25], ["as", 2.261, 2.33], ["not", 2.33, 2.591], ["everyone", 2.602, 3.011], ["wants", 3.011, 3.182], ["their", 3.182, 3.273], ["money", 3.284, 3.557], ["back", 3.557, 3.852], ["on", 3.852, 3.909], ["the", 3.909, 3.966], ["same", 3.966, 4.227], ["day", 4.227, 4.58]]}, {"text": "When they do, it's called a bank run. And history shows how brutal that can get.", "start": 49.91, "end": 54.734, "spec": {"type": "img", "img": 3, "mood": "tense"}, "words": [["When", 0.091, 0.17], ["they", 0.182, 0.273], ["do", 0.273, 0.614], ["it's", 0.841, 0.909], ["called", 0.909, 1.091], ["a", 1.091, 1.148], ["bank", 1.159, 1.5], ["run", 1.5, 1.818], ["And", 2.205, 2.295], ["history", 2.295, 2.693], ["shows", 2.705, 3.034], ["how", 3.034, 3.25], ["brutal", 3.375, 3.909], ["that", 3.909, 4.045], ["can", 4.045, 4.148], ["get", 4.159, 4.477]]}, {"text": "Between nineteen thirty and nineteen thirty-three, around nine thousand American banks shut their doors.", "start": 55.134, "end": 61.206, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-97, 38.5, 3.2], "view": "us", "dots": true, "counter": {"to": 9000, "label": "banks suspended, 1930–1933", "pre": "", "suf": ""}}, "words": [["Between", 0.091, 0.352], ["nineteen", 0.352, 0.773], ["thirty", 0.773, 1.227], ["and", 1.295, 1.398], ["nineteen", 1.398, 1.841], ["thirty-three", 1.841, 2.5], ["around", 2.75, 3.102], ["nine", 3.239, 3.557], ["thousand", 3.568, 3.92], ["American", 3.92, 4.239], ["banks", 4.25, 4.636], ["shut", 4.795, 5.068], ["their", 5.068, 5.193], ["doors", 5.205, 5.727]]}, {"text": "Millions of families lost their savings, because back then, nothing protected their deposits.", "start": 61.606, "end": 66.43, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-97, 38.5, 3.2], "view": "us", "dots": true, "fade": true}, "words": [["Millions", 0.08, 0.432], ["of", 0.432, 0.5], ["families", 0.5, 0.966], ["lost", 0.966, 1.307], ["their", 1.318, 1.432], ["savings", 1.432, 1.955], ["because", 1.966, 2.227], ["back", 2.227, 2.534], ["then", 2.545, 2.795], ["nothing", 3.045, 3.284], ["protected", 3.284, 3.739], ["their", 3.739, 3.841], ["deposits", 3.841, 4.5]]}, {"text": "And it's not just history. In two thousand seven, people lined up outside Northern Rock in Britain. It was the first bank run in the UK since Victorian times.", "start": 66.83, "end": 75.878, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-1.6, 54.97, 9], "pins": [{"at": [-1.61, 54.98], "label": "Northern Rock · 2007", "col": "red"}], "photo": 8, "hl": ["GBR"]}, "words": [["And", 0.091, 0.125], ["it's", 0.125, 0.216], ["not", 0.227, 0.398], ["just", 0.398, 0.591], ["history", 0.591, 1.045], ["In", 1.409, 1.489], ["two", 1.489, 1.636], ["thousand", 1.636, 1.932], ["seven", 1.943, 2.341], ["people", 2.716, 3.0], ["lined", 3.0, 3.25], ["up", 3.25, 3.375], ["outside", 3.455, 3.943], ["Northern", 3.955, 4.307], ["Rock", 4.318, 4.591], ["in", 4.602, 4.67], ["Britain", 4.682, 5.023], ["It", 5.398, 5.443], ["was", 5.455, 5.545], ["the", 5.557, 5.625], ["first", 5.625, 5.943], ["bank", 5.943, 6.227], ["run", 6.227, 6.545], ["in", 6.557, 6.648], ["the", 6.659, 6.693], ["UK", 6.693, 7.284], ["since", 7.477, 7.67], ["Victorian", 7.682, 8.136], ["times", 8.136, 8.705]]}, {"text": "So in nineteen thirty-three, the US created the FDIC. Its deposit insurance started on January first, nineteen thirty-four.", "start": 76.278, "end": 84.63, "spec": {"type": "shield", "step": "fdic", "mood": "calm"}, "words": [["So", 0.091, 0.216], ["in", 0.216, 0.273], ["nineteen", 0.273, 0.659], ["thirty-three", 0.659, 1.261], ["the", 1.591, 1.648], ["US", 1.648, 2.045], ["created", 2.057, 2.477], ["the", 2.489, 2.568], ["FDIC", 2.568, 3.409], ["Its", 3.784, 3.875], ["deposit", 3.875, 4.375], ["insurance", 4.375, 4.966], ["started", 5.136, 5.534], ["on", 5.534, 5.648], ["January", 5.659, 6.136], ["first", 6.148, 6.716], ["nineteen", 6.92, 7.375], ["thirty-four", 7.375, 8.0]]}, {"text": "Today, it covers two hundred fifty thousand dollars per person, per bank, per account type.", "start": 85.03, "end": 89.662, "spec": {"type": "shield", "step": "limit"}, "words": [["Today", 0.091, 0.375], ["it", 0.386, 0.477], ["covers", 0.477, 0.807], ["two", 0.807, 0.989], ["hundred", 0.989, 1.193], ["fifty", 1.205, 1.455], ["thousand", 1.466, 1.807], ["dollars", 1.818, 2.114], ["per", 2.125, 2.273], ["person", 2.284, 2.773], ["per", 2.955, 3.148], ["bank", 3.159, 3.545], ["per", 3.557, 3.693], ["account", 3.693, 3.977], ["type", 3.977, 4.307]]}, {"text": "And since nineteen thirty-four, no depositor has lost a single penny of insured money.", "start": 90.062, "end": 95.054, "spec": {"type": "shield", "step": "zero"}, "words": [["And", 0.094, 0.177], ["since", 0.177, 0.354], ["nineteen", 0.354, 0.755], ["thirty-four", 0.755, 1.38], ["no", 1.804, 1.993], ["depositor", 1.993, 2.535], ["has", 2.535, 2.677], ["lost", 2.677, 2.995], ["a", 3.007, 3.054], ["single", 3.066, 3.479], ["penny", 3.479, 3.809], ["of", 3.809, 3.891], ["insured", 3.892, 4.316], ["money", 4.316, 4.658]]}, {"text": "Other countries do the same. The European Union protects one hundred thousand euros, and the UK, one hundred twenty thousand pounds.", "start": 95.454, "end": 103.062, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-40, 45, 1.25], "pins": [{"at": [-98, 39], "label": "USA · $250,000", "col": "green"}, {"at": [16, 47.5], "label": "EU · €100,000", "col": "green", "dy": -0.6}, {"at": [-2, 53.5], "label": "UK · £120,000", "col": "green", "dy": 1.3}], "hl": ["USA", "GBR", "EU"]}, "words": [["Other", 0.08, 0.239], ["countries", 0.239, 0.636], ["do", 0.636, 0.761], ["the", 0.761, 0.83], ["same", 0.83, 1.239], ["The", 1.614, 1.659], ["European", 1.659, 2.148], ["Union", 2.148, 2.443], ["protects", 2.443, 2.92], ["one", 2.932, 3.136], ["hundred", 3.136, 3.5], ["thousand", 3.511, 3.886], ["euros", 3.886, 4.386], ["and", 4.591, 4.67], ["the", 4.67, 4.716], ["UK", 4.716, 5.261], ["one", 5.693, 5.784], ["hundred", 5.784, 6.114], ["twenty", 6.125, 6.375], ["thousand", 6.375, 6.727], ["pounds", 6.727, 7.273]]}, {"text": "So why did Silicon Valley Bank still turn into a disaster?", "start": 103.662, "end": 106.998, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-121.96, 37.35, 6.5], "pins": [{"at": [-121.96, 37.35], "label": "Silicon Valley Bank", "col": "red"}], "mood": "tense"}, "words": [["So", 0.091, 0.25], ["why", 0.25, 0.409], ["did", 0.42, 0.545], ["Silicon", 0.545, 0.898], ["Valley", 0.898, 1.159], ["Bank", 1.159, 1.5], ["still", 1.511, 1.955], ["turn", 1.966, 2.148], ["into", 2.159, 2.352], ["a", 2.352, 2.386], ["disaster", 2.386, 3.0]]}, {"text": "Its customers were mostly startups and tech companies, with accounts far above the limit. About eighty-six percent of its deposits were not insured.", "start": 107.398, "end": 115.438, "spec": {"type": "pie", "v": 86.4}, "words": [["Its", 0.08, 0.17], ["customers", 0.17, 0.591], ["were", 0.602, 0.705], ["mostly", 0.705, 1.182], ["startups", 1.182, 1.818], ["and", 1.92, 2.045], ["tech", 2.045, 2.318], ["companies", 2.318, 2.83], ["with", 3.023, 3.136], ["accounts", 3.136, 3.477], ["far", 3.477, 3.739], ["above", 3.739, 4.011], ["the", 4.011, 4.08], ["limit", 4.091, 4.455], ["About", 4.818, 5.068], ["eighty-six", 5.08, 5.5], ["percent", 5.5, 5.966], ["of", 6.057, 6.136], ["its", 6.136, 6.227], ["deposits", 6.239, 6.773], ["were", 6.784, 6.886], ["not", 6.898, 7.193], ["insured", 7.193, 7.705]]}, {"text": "The bank had put a huge part of that money into long-term bonds. Then interest rates shot up, and those bonds lost value.", "start": 115.838, "end": 122.75, "spec": {"type": "bond"}, "words": [["The", 0.102, 0.17], ["bank", 0.17, 0.432], ["had", 0.443, 0.545], ["put", 0.545, 0.636], ["a", 0.636, 0.659], ["huge", 0.67, 1.125], ["part", 1.136, 1.307], ["of", 1.318, 1.352], ["that", 1.352, 1.523], ["money", 1.523, 1.909], ["into", 1.989, 2.125], ["long-term", 2.125, 2.67], ["bonds", 2.67, 3.17], ["Then", 3.545, 3.67], ["interest", 3.739, 4.045], ["rates", 4.057, 4.239], ["shot", 4.25, 4.545], ["up", 4.545, 4.727], ["and", 5.17, 5.25], ["those", 5.25, 5.489], ["bonds", 5.489, 5.875], ["lost", 5.886, 6.159], ["value", 6.17, 6.591]]}, {"text": "Selling them now would mean locking in those losses. Keeping them meant the bank had less cash on hand than it looked.", "start": 123.15, "end": 129.702, "spec": {"type": "bond", "step": 2}, "words": [["Selling", 0.091, 0.386], ["them", 0.398, 0.5], ["now", 0.5, 0.898], ["would", 1.011, 1.159], ["mean", 1.159, 1.409], ["locking", 1.42, 1.875], ["in", 1.875, 1.943], ["those", 1.943, 2.136], ["losses", 2.136, 2.75], ["Keeping", 3.114, 3.352], ["them", 3.352, 3.5], ["meant", 3.648, 3.807], ["the", 3.807, 3.898], ["bank", 3.898, 4.239], ["had", 4.25, 4.455], ["less", 4.466, 4.716], ["cash", 4.716, 5.091], ["on", 5.102, 5.216], ["hand", 5.227, 5.682], ["than", 5.693, 5.784], ["it", 5.784, 5.864], ["looked", 5.875, 6.239]]}, {"text": "On March eighth, the bank admitted that it had sold bonds at a one point eight billion dollar loss, and that it needed to raise new money.", "start": 130.102, "end": 137.518, "spec": {"type": "loss"}, "words": [["On", 0.08, 0.182], ["March", 0.182, 0.489], ["eighth", 0.489, 0.92], ["the", 1.08, 1.182], ["bank", 1.182, 1.455], ["admitted", 1.466, 1.795], ["that", 1.795, 1.886], ["it", 1.886, 1.932], ["had", 1.943, 2.102], ["sold", 2.102, 2.455], ["bonds", 2.455, 2.966], ["at", 3.057, 3.136], ["a", 3.136, 3.182], ["one", 3.182, 3.545], ["point", 3.557, 3.864], ["eight", 3.943, 4.239], ["billion", 4.25, 4.545], ["dollar", 4.545, 4.818], ["loss", 4.818, 5.273], ["and", 5.614, 5.67], ["that", 5.67, 5.761], ["it", 5.761, 5.841], ["needed", 5.841, 6.102], ["to", 6.102, 6.17], ["raise", 6.17, 6.523], ["new", 6.534, 6.693], ["money", 6.693, 7.08]]}, {"text": "Founders warned each other in group chats and on social media. Within hours, everyone tried to get out at once.", "start": 137.918, "end": 143.966, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-98, 39, 1.25], "view": "us", "spread": true}, "words": [["Founders", 0.148, 0.443], ["warned", 0.455, 0.761], ["each", 0.761, 0.909], ["other", 0.909, 1.08], ["in", 1.091, 1.159], ["group", 1.17, 1.42], ["chats", 1.42, 1.841], ["and", 2.068, 2.182], ["on", 2.193, 2.307], ["social", 2.307, 2.614], ["media", 2.614, 3.023], ["Within", 3.398, 3.602], ["hours", 3.602, 4.125], ["everyone", 4.364, 4.648], ["tried", 4.648, 4.852], ["to", 4.864, 4.898], ["get", 4.898, 5.011], ["out", 5.011, 5.114], ["at", 5.125, 5.182], ["once", 5.182, 5.693]]}, {"text": "In just two days, customers tried to pull out about eighty-one percent of all deposits. And this time, nobody had to stand in line. They just tapped a button.", "start": 144.366, "end": 153.294, "spec": {"type": "bar81"}, "words": [["In", 0.068, 0.136], ["just", 0.136, 0.284], ["two", 0.284, 0.443], ["days", 0.455, 0.989], ["customers", 1.17, 1.659], ["tried", 1.67, 1.898], ["to", 1.898, 1.955], ["pull", 1.955, 2.193], ["out", 2.205, 2.386], ["about", 2.398, 2.659], ["eighty-one", 2.795, 3.17], ["percent", 3.182, 3.727], ["of", 3.932, 4.034], ["all", 4.125, 4.25], ["deposits", 4.25, 4.92], ["And", 5.284, 5.386], ["this", 5.455, 5.591], ["time", 5.602, 5.943], ["nobody", 6.352, 6.602], ["had", 6.602, 6.761], ["to", 6.761, 6.795], ["stand", 6.807, 7.091], ["in", 7.091, 7.182], ["line", 7.193, 7.523], ["They", 7.898, 7.943], ["just", 7.943, 8.08], ["tapped", 8.091, 8.295], ["a", 8.295, 8.33], ["button", 8.33, 8.614]]}, {"text": "On March tenth, regulators shut it down. It was the third-largest bank failure in American history.", "start": 153.694, "end": 159.67, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-121.96, 37.35, 6.5], "pins": [{"at": [-121.96, 37.35], "label": "Silicon Valley Bank", "col": "red", "closed": true}]}, "words": [["On", 0.091, 0.17], ["March", 0.17, 0.466], ["tenth", 0.477, 0.92], ["regulators", 1.148, 1.682], ["shut", 1.784, 1.955], ["it", 1.955, 2.023], ["down", 2.023, 2.33], ["It", 2.693, 2.739], ["was", 2.739, 2.83], ["the", 2.83, 2.92], ["third-largest", 2.92, 3.795], ["bank", 3.807, 4.068], ["failure", 4.08, 4.625], ["in", 4.716, 4.795], ["American", 4.795, 5.136], ["history", 5.136, 5.625]]}, {"text": "And suddenly, real companies had their cash stuck inside. The streaming company Roku had about four hundred eighty-seven million dollars there. That was a quarter of all its cash.", "start": 160.07, "end": 169.91, "spec": {"type": "stuck", "step": 1}, "words": [["And", 0.091, 0.193], ["suddenly", 0.205, 0.693], ["real", 0.909, 1.114], ["companies", 1.114, 1.511], ["had", 1.523, 1.625], ["their", 1.636, 1.739], ["cash", 1.739, 2.114], ["stuck", 2.125, 2.364], ["inside", 2.364, 2.875], ["The", 3.239, 3.295], ["streaming", 3.295, 3.67], ["company", 3.67, 3.966], ["Roku", 3.966, 4.466], ["had", 4.727, 4.92], ["about", 4.92, 5.159], ["four", 5.17, 5.511], ["hundred", 5.511, 5.886], ["eighty-seven", 6.023, 6.568], ["million", 6.568, 6.864], ["dollars", 6.875, 7.227], ["there", 7.239, 7.545], ["That", 7.909, 7.977], ["was", 7.977, 8.08], ["a", 8.08, 8.148], ["quarter", 8.159, 8.534], ["of", 8.534, 8.614], ["all", 8.625, 8.83], ["its", 8.83, 8.92], ["cash", 8.932, 9.511]]}, {"text": "The crypto company Circle had three point three billion dollars stuck. Its digital dollar, which is supposed to be worth exactly one dollar, fell below eighty-seven cents.", "start": 170.31, "end": 180.39, "spec": {"type": "stuck", "step": 2}, "words": [["The", 0.091, 0.136], ["crypto", 0.148, 0.432], ["company", 0.443, 0.739], ["Circle", 0.75, 1.182], ["had", 1.193, 1.432], ["three", 1.557, 1.852], ["point", 1.864, 2.182], ["three", 2.193, 2.648], ["billion", 2.784, 3.114], ["dollars", 3.114, 3.432], ["stuck", 3.432, 3.818], ["Its", 4.193, 4.307], ["digital", 4.318, 4.682], ["dollar", 4.693, 5.08], ["which", 5.091, 5.216], ["is", 5.227, 5.295], ["supposed", 5.295, 5.67], ["to", 5.67, 5.716], ["be", 5.727, 5.83], ["worth", 5.83, 6.159], ["exactly", 6.227, 6.841], ["one", 6.841, 7.091], ["dollar", 7.102, 7.511], ["fell", 7.886, 8.08], ["below", 8.08, 8.5], ["eighty-seven", 8.693, 9.193], ["cents", 9.193, 9.739]]}, {"text": "Then came the weekend that saved everyone.", "start": 181.04, "end": 183.8, "spec": {"type": "img", "img": 5, "mood": "bright", "cut": true}, "words": [["Then", 0.091, 0.261], ["came", 0.261, 0.443], ["the", 0.443, 0.534], ["weekend", 0.534, 1.045], ["that", 1.239, 1.364], ["saved", 1.364, 1.864], ["everyone", 1.977, 2.42]]}, {"text": "On March twelfth, the government decided that all depositors would get their money back, even above the limit. And it was paid for with a special fee on other banks.", "start": 184.2, "end": 193.248, "spec": {"type": "rescue"}, "words": [["On", 0.08, 0.17], ["March", 0.17, 0.42], ["twelfth", 0.42, 0.955], ["the", 1.318, 1.409], ["government", 1.42, 1.852], ["decided", 1.864, 2.364], ["that", 2.375, 2.523], ["all", 2.534, 2.727], ["depositors", 2.739, 3.352], ["would", 3.364, 3.534], ["get", 3.534, 3.693], ["their", 3.705, 3.795], ["money", 3.795, 4.091], ["back", 4.091, 4.489], ["even", 4.909, 5.114], ["above", 5.114, 5.42], ["the", 5.432, 5.511], ["limit", 5.511, 5.864], ["And", 6.227, 6.273], ["it", 6.273, 6.318], ["was", 6.318, 6.432], ["paid", 6.432, 6.67], ["for", 6.682, 6.807], ["with", 6.807, 6.92], ["a", 6.92, 6.955], ["special", 6.955, 7.364], ["fee", 7.375, 7.761], ["on", 7.773, 7.977], ["other", 7.989, 8.17], ["banks", 8.182, 8.716]]}, {"text": "But the fear kept spreading. Signature Bank in New York fell that same weekend, and in May, First Republic in San Francisco collapsed too.", "start": 193.648, "end": 202.216, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-98, 39, 1.25], "view": "us", "pins": [{"at": [-121.96, 37.35], "label": "Silicon Valley Bank", "col": "red", "closed": true}, {"at": [-74.0, 40.71], "label": "Signature Bank", "col": "red", "closed": true}, {"at": [-122.42, 37.77], "label": "First Republic", "col": "red", "closed": true, "dy": 1, "delay": 0.55}], "mood": "tense"}, "words": [["But", 0.091, 0.17], ["the", 0.182, 0.25], ["fear", 0.25, 0.818], ["kept", 0.966, 1.239], ["spreading", 1.25, 1.761], ["Signature", 2.114, 2.523], ["Bank", 2.523, 2.852], ["in", 2.864, 3.0], ["New", 3.011, 3.125], ["York", 3.125, 3.318], ["fell", 3.318, 3.614], ["that", 3.625, 3.761], ["same", 3.761, 4.102], ["weekend", 4.102, 4.58], ["and", 4.966, 5.057], ["in", 5.068, 5.182], ["May", 5.182, 5.545], ["First", 5.932, 6.182], ["Republic", 6.182, 6.602], ["in", 6.67, 6.773], ["San", 6.784, 7.045], ["Francisco", 7.045, 7.545], ["collapsed", 7.545, 7.943], ["too", 7.943, 8.239]]}, {"text": "With two hundred twenty-nine billion dollars in assets, First Republic became the second-largest bank failure ever in the US.", "start": 202.616, "end": 209.576, "spec": {"type": "rank"}, "words": [["With", 0.091, 0.182], ["two", 0.193, 0.375], ["hundred", 0.375, 0.523], ["twenty-nine", 0.523, 0.886], ["billion", 0.898, 1.17], ["dollars", 1.17, 1.5], ["in", 1.511, 1.591], ["assets", 1.602, 2.193], ["First", 2.545, 2.852], ["Republic", 2.852, 3.205], ["became", 3.216, 3.534], ["the", 3.534, 3.602], ["second-largest", 3.614, 4.409], ["bank", 4.42, 4.716], ["failure", 4.795, 5.307], ["ever", 5.443, 5.739], ["in", 5.852, 5.943], ["the", 5.955, 5.989], ["US", 6.0, 6.614]]}, {"text": "And then, the fear jumped across the Atlantic.", "start": 209.976, "end": 213.072, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-40, 45, 1.25], "arc": {"a": [-98, 39], "b": [8.54, 47.37]}, "pins": [{"at": [8.54, 47.37], "label": "Zurich", "col": "gold"}]}, "words": [["And", 0.091, 0.205], ["then", 0.216, 0.489], ["the", 0.83, 0.92], ["fear", 0.92, 1.261], ["jumped", 1.398, 1.716], ["across", 1.716, 2.125], ["the", 2.125, 2.227], ["Atlantic", 2.239, 2.761]]}, {"text": "Credit Suisse, a hundred sixty-seven year old Swiss bank, had to be rescued. On March nineteenth, its rival UBS bought it for just three billion Swiss francs.", "start": 213.472, "end": 223.816, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [8.4, 46.8, 14], "hl": ["CHE"], "pins": [{"at": [8.54, 47.37], "label": "Credit Suisse · since 1856", "col": "red", "closed": true}], "counter": {"to": 3, "pre": "CHF ", "suf": "B", "label": "sale price to UBS"}}, "words": [["Credit", 0.091, 0.341], ["Suisse", 0.341, 0.955], ["a", 1.17, 1.205], ["hundred", 1.375, 1.682], ["sixty-seven", 1.682, 2.341], ["year", 2.352, 2.648], ["old", 2.716, 2.955], ["Swiss", 2.955, 3.295], ["bank", 3.295, 3.614], ["had", 3.943, 4.057], ["to", 4.057, 4.091], ["be", 4.091, 4.216], ["rescued", 4.227, 4.75], ["On", 5.125, 5.205], ["March", 5.205, 5.443], ["nineteenth", 5.455, 6.102], ["its", 6.284, 6.409], ["rival", 6.42, 6.739], ["UBS", 6.739, 7.364], ["bought", 7.375, 7.636], ["it", 7.636, 7.739], ["for", 7.875, 8.023], ["just", 8.023, 8.295], ["three", 8.307, 8.784], ["billion", 8.875, 9.227], ["Swiss", 9.239, 9.489], ["francs", 9.489, 9.989]]}, {"text": "And some investors lost everything. Sixteen billion francs in special bonds were written down to zero.", "start": 224.216, "end": 230.48, "spec": {"type": "at1"}, "words": [["And", 0.091, 0.318], ["some", 0.534, 0.659], ["investors", 0.659, 1.17], ["lost", 1.17, 1.648], ["everything", 1.659, 2.136], ["Sixteen", 2.511, 2.966], ["billion", 2.966, 3.284], ["francs", 3.295, 3.716], ["in", 3.727, 3.795], ["special", 3.807, 4.17], ["bonds", 4.182, 4.58], ["were", 4.591, 4.75], ["written", 4.761, 4.977], ["down", 4.977, 5.318], ["to", 5.33, 5.42], ["zero", 5.42, 5.92]]}, {"text": "So, what happens to your money if your bank fails?", "start": 231.08, "end": 233.912, "spec": {"type": "img", "img": 7, "mood": "calm"}, "words": [["So", 0.091, 0.273], ["what", 0.75, 0.841], ["happens", 0.841, 1.125], ["to", 1.125, 1.205], ["your", 1.205, 1.273], ["money", 1.273, 1.534], ["if", 1.545, 1.625], ["your", 1.625, 1.705], ["bank", 1.716, 1.989], ["fails", 1.989, 2.489]]}, {"text": "If you're under the limit, usually almost nothing. Most of the time, a healthy bank takes over your account, and you can use your money right away.", "start": 234.312, "end": 241.68, "spec": {"type": "transfer"}, "words": [["If", 0.091, 0.182], ["you're", 0.182, 0.261], ["under", 0.261, 0.398], ["the", 0.398, 0.477], ["limit", 0.477, 0.795], ["usually", 1.057, 1.386], ["almost", 1.398, 1.739], ["nothing", 1.75, 2.205], ["Most", 2.545, 2.727], ["of", 2.727, 2.773], ["the", 2.773, 2.83], ["time", 2.841, 3.239], ["a", 3.648, 3.67], ["healthy", 3.682, 4.08], ["bank", 4.08, 4.398], ["takes", 4.409, 4.705], ["over", 4.705, 4.864], ["your", 4.864, 5.0], ["account", 5.0, 5.398], ["and", 5.795, 5.864], ["you", 5.875, 5.955], ["can", 5.955, 6.08], ["use", 6.08, 6.25], ["your", 6.25, 6.33], ["money", 6.33, 6.534], ["right", 6.534, 6.682], ["away", 6.682, 7.045]]}, {"text": "If no bank steps in, the FDIC sends you a check, and payments usually begin within a few days.", "start": 242.08, "end": 248.08, "spec": {"type": "check"}, "words": [["If", 0.091, 0.216], ["no", 0.227, 0.432], ["bank", 0.443, 0.716], ["steps", 0.716, 1.102], ["in", 1.102, 1.318], ["the", 1.648, 1.75], ["FDIC", 1.761, 2.511], ["sends", 2.523, 2.807], ["you", 2.807, 2.898], ["a", 2.898, 2.932], ["check", 2.932, 3.364], ["and", 3.625, 3.727], ["payments", 3.727, 4.125], ["usually", 4.136, 4.466], ["begin", 4.466, 4.773], ["within", 4.773, 4.989], ["a", 5.0, 5.023], ["few", 5.023, 5.227], ["days", 5.227, 5.659]]}, {"text": "Only the money above the limit is at risk. You become a creditor of the failed bank, and you might get some of it back, or not.", "start": 248.48, "end": 255.296, "spec": {"type": "above"}, "words": [["Only", 0.091, 0.284], ["the", 0.284, 0.352], ["money", 0.364, 0.693], ["above", 0.693, 0.966], ["the", 0.966, 1.045], ["limit", 1.045, 1.375], ["is", 1.477, 1.614], ["at", 1.625, 1.739], ["risk", 1.739, 2.216], ["You", 2.58, 2.648], ["become", 2.648, 2.875], ["a", 2.875, 2.932], ["creditor", 2.932, 3.409], ["of", 3.409, 3.466], ["the", 3.466, 3.523], ["failed", 3.534, 3.932], ["bank", 3.932, 4.295], ["and", 4.705, 4.739], ["you", 4.739, 4.818], ["might", 4.818, 5.045], ["get", 5.045, 5.182], ["some", 5.193, 5.364], ["of", 5.364, 5.42], ["it", 5.42, 5.489], ["back", 5.489, 5.875], ["or", 6.023, 6.102], ["not", 6.102, 6.477]]}, {"text": "So here's what you can do. First, keep your savings under the limit at each bank. If you have more, spread it across several banks.", "start": 255.696, "end": 262.944, "spec": {"type": "tips", "n": 1, "img": 6, "mood": "bright"}, "words": [["So", 0.091, 0.193], ["here's", 0.193, 0.42], ["what", 0.42, 0.511], ["you", 0.523, 0.602], ["can", 0.602, 0.693], ["do", 0.693, 0.966], ["First", 1.352, 1.807], ["keep", 2.011, 2.193], ["your", 2.193, 2.295], ["savings", 2.307, 2.784], ["under", 2.784, 2.92], ["the", 2.92, 2.989], ["limit", 3.0, 3.273], ["at", 3.284, 3.386], ["each", 3.398, 3.58], ["bank", 3.591, 3.989], ["If", 4.33, 4.42], ["you", 4.432, 4.489], ["have", 4.489, 4.693], ["more", 4.693, 5.102], ["spread", 5.33, 5.602], ["it", 5.602, 5.67], ["across", 5.682, 6.023], ["several", 6.023, 6.398], ["banks", 6.409, 6.909]]}, {"text": "Second, make sure your bank is actually insured. Some apps look like banks, but they aren't banks themselves.", "start": 263.344, "end": 269.68, "spec": {"type": "tips", "n": 2, "img": 6}, "words": [["Second", 0.102, 0.5], ["make", 0.898, 1.023], ["sure", 1.023, 1.182], ["your", 1.193, 1.295], ["bank", 1.307, 1.659], ["is", 1.932, 2.045], ["actually", 2.057, 2.432], ["insured", 2.432, 2.92], ["Some", 3.295, 3.443], ["apps", 3.443, 3.614], ["look", 3.614, 3.739], ["like", 3.739, 3.92], ["banks", 3.932, 4.455], ["but", 4.636, 4.739], ["they", 4.75, 4.852], ["aren't", 4.852, 5.068], ["banks", 5.068, 5.307], ["themselves", 5.318, 5.989]]}, {"text": "And third, don't panic. Bank runs are what kill banks. Your insured money is safe, even when the headlines look scary.", "start": 270.08, "end": 277.808, "spec": {"type": "tips", "n": 3, "img": 6}, "words": [["And", 0.091, 0.205], ["third", 0.409, 0.83], ["don't", 0.932, 1.125], ["panic", 1.125, 1.534], ["Bank", 1.909, 2.114], ["runs", 2.125, 2.42], ["are", 2.42, 2.534], ["what", 2.534, 2.716], ["kill", 2.716, 2.955], ["banks", 2.955, 3.477], ["Your", 3.83, 3.955], ["insured", 3.955, 4.352], ["money", 4.352, 4.773], ["is", 4.784, 4.92], ["safe", 4.92, 5.42], ["even", 5.875, 6.091], ["when", 6.091, 6.182], ["the", 6.182, 6.239], ["headlines", 6.25, 6.75], ["look", 6.75, 6.864], ["scary", 6.875, 7.409]]}, {"text": "Would you have pulled your money out of Silicon Valley Bank? Tell me in the comments.", "start": 278.208, "end": 282.048, "spec": {"type": "img", "img": 4, "chips": ["Yes", "No"]}, "words": [["Would", 0.091, 0.193], ["you", 0.193, 0.25], ["have", 0.25, 0.341], ["pulled", 0.352, 0.568], ["your", 0.58, 0.682], ["money", 0.682, 1.068], ["out", 1.08, 1.25], ["of", 1.25, 1.307], ["Silicon", 1.307, 1.659], ["Valley", 1.659, 1.864], ["Bank", 1.864, 2.227], ["Tell", 2.591, 2.693], ["me", 2.705, 2.795], ["in", 2.795, 2.841], ["the", 2.852, 2.898], ["comments", 2.898, 3.5]]}, {"text": "And subscribe for more money explained simply.", "start": 282.448, "end": 284.776, "spec": {"type": "outro", "mood": "calm"}, "words": [["And", 0.091, 0.148], ["subscribe", 0.159, 0.568], ["for", 0.568, 0.67], ["more", 0.67, 0.875], ["money", 0.875, 1.136], ["explained", 1.148, 1.58], ["simply", 1.58, 2.0]]}], "dur": 287.78}